{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MarkovZToCkMapping","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovZToCkMapping","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovParameterRecursion","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ToroidalHarmonicsBasis"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.fmap_c2_is_minus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.fmap_c2_is_minus_one","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZToCkMapping.lean#L61-L71","doc":"If the f-map bridges to the categorical ladder, then the resulting $c_2$ must be -1.\nThis is a sanity check that the f-map commutes with the known Kashiwara $c_2$ bound.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ZToCkMappingClass.f_map_bridges_to_ck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ZToCkMappingClass.f_map_bridges_to_ck","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZToCkMapping.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The f-map maps the real-embedded $a_n$ Markov coefficients to the $c_k(q)$ sequence\nat every evaluated $q > 0$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ZToCkMappingClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ZToCkMappingClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZToCkMapping.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ZToCkMappingClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ZToCkMappingClass","kind":"class","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZToCkMapping.lean#L44-L59","doc":"**Z to C_k Mapping Class** (§3b-cond open f-map)\n\nAxiomatises the structure of the map from the pre-archimedean $z$-recursion \ncoefficients ($a_n$) to the Q_β precision ladder categorical coefficients $c_k(q)$.\n\nThe mapping evaluates the formal sequence against the specific substrate anchor \n$q$, producing the rung parameters $c_k(q)$ defined in `QBetaPrecisionLadderCoefficients`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qBetaFMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qBetaFMap","kind":"opaque","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZToCkMapping.lean#L35-L42","doc":"The abstract f-map from the Markov $a_n$ coefficients to the Q_β ladder \n$c_k$ coefficients. It is parametrised by $q$ since the categorical \nderivation (e.g. Hexagon equations) introduces $q$-dependent weights. ","signatureChunk":0}]}